WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.356
The exposure check runs the guide's two
queries: high and critical vulnerabilities

2
00:00:05.356 --> 00:00:10.200
by software and recommended update,
and exposed or internet-facing devices.

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.994
It matches each exposed
device's group to a

4
00:00:12.994 --> 00:00:16.187
remediation owner from
the agency's owners file.

5
00:00:16.187 --> 00:00:21.425
A device with no owner is an inventory
finding, not just a vulnerability finding.

6
00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:24.575
And it writes the disposition
for the settings file's cloud.

7
00:00:24.575 --> 00:00:28.315
For GCC: not available,
skipped, not applicable,

8
00:00:28.315 --> 00:00:31.562
with the interim path and the Learn page.

9
00:00:31.562 --> 00:00:36.260
That result name is one of the seven the
Zero Trust Assessment results kit uses,

10
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.580
so the same disposition lands
in the closure register.
